  "title": "AEG Dryer",
  "revisionid": 1480040,
  "contents_raw": "== Background ==\n\nEngineer Emil Rathenau founded AEG, a German electrical equipment and appliance manufacturer in 1883. The company released its first clothes dryer in 1964. AEG dryers often come equipped with ProSteam and AbsoluteCare technology. Today, Swedish appliance manufacturer Electrolux owns AEG.\n\n== Identification ==\n\nThe model number can be found inside the dryer, around the drum. Common models include the T7DBK841N, T8DEE945R, and the T9DEB969C.\n\n== Additional Resources ==\n\n* [link|https://www.aeg.co.uk/support/user-manuals/|AEG Owner's Manuals]",
